# Copy to /etc/kajianq/api.env on the VPS: `install -o root -g root -m 0600`.
# This is the staging-deployment template — the recorded posture — and a rebuild
# installs it verbatim (`docs/VPS-SETUP.md`), so its `APP_ENV` is the only place
# a fresh box takes its label from.
# Read by systemd as `EnvironmentFile` for kajianq-api.service AND
# kajianq-cron.service — this one file is the serving process's whole
# configuration (plus the cron entry's, which reads the same DATABASE_URL).
# Never commit the filled-in file. Every value below is a placeholder; the real
# ones live in the owner's password manager.
#
# The keys mirror apps/api/src/lib/server.ts's PASSTHROUGH_KEYS exactly
# (tests/scripts/vps-hardening.test.mjs pins the two in sync) — read once at
# the composition root; business logic never touches env.* directly.
#
# DATABASE_URL         the self-hosted Postgres (loopback; ADR-0044 decision 5).
#                      Password required: over TCP, md5/scram auth applies.
# APP_ENV              "staging" — the recorded posture: one deployment
#                      labeled `staging`, production deferred (ADR-0044
#                      decision 2; deferred 2026-10-03). Provisioning production
#                      is a new decision and a new host (ADR-0044's revisit
#                      trigger), never an edit to this line, which only
#                      relabels this box; the value drives log posture only —
#                      log labels and the health JSON.
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS      the strict CORS allowlist — the public origin.
# SENTRY_DSN           optional; omit to disable error reporting.
#
# Provider keys. An absent key means that role's keyed candidates are
# filtered out at wiring — for the REVIEWER and EMBEDDER chain heads this
# takes the whole chat path down with a typed error, so these two are
# owner-provisioned preconditions of the cutover (the enforcement test
# apps/api/src/lib/personal-data-serving.test.ts pins the config side):
#   GEMINI_PAID_API_KEY  the embedder head (gemini-paid:gemini-embedding-001)
#   GEMINI_API_KEY       the cheap-role free-tier candidate (filtered for
#                        personal-data calls; kept for parity with the config)
#   DEEPSEEK_API_KEY     the generator/router AND reviewer paid head
#                        (same-vendor review accepted by owner decision, 2026-09-21;
#                        ADR-0044 decision 7)
#   DASHSCOPE_API_KEY    catalogued generator challenger (optional)
#   OLLAMA_API_KEY       the switchable chat vendor's key (ADR-0059): required
#                        only when `PROVIDER_PROFILE=ollama` routes the
#                        generator/reviewer/cheap roles to it. With that profile
#                        selected and this key absent, each such call fails with
#                        a typed provider error naming this variable — there is
#                        no silent fallback to DeepSeek. Absent by default.
#   JEV_API_KEY          the decision vendor's serving key: binds the reviewer
#                        pre-gate (#168, ADR-0042). Optional and fail-open — an
#                        absent key means the reviewer runs on every answer
#                        exactly as before adoption, so it is never a boot
#                        precondition. Bound = the pre-gate is active (no
#                        enable flag exists; owner decision 2026-09-19).
#
# PROVIDER_PROFILE     the named provider profile from models.json (ADR-0059).
#                      `default` (or removing the line) = the DeepSeek chains
#                      above; `ollama` re-heads generator, reviewer,
#                      reviewer-live and the cheap chain on Ollama Cloud and
#                      leaves the embedder, translation and decision vendor
#                      untouched. An unknown name is a typed config failure at
#                      wiring time (the boot posture report fails the process),
#                      never a silent default. Switch: set the two values and
#                      restart kajianq-api. Roll back: remove this line and
#                      restart — no JSON edit, no revert commit.
#
# SCOPE_EXPANSION_CAP  ADR-0045's surah-read budget: the most children of a surah
#                      added to the fused hits — the surah a question names and a
#                      retrieved verse's short surah share it (non-negative
#                      integer; `0` disables the reads; absent = the domain
#                      default of 12; a malformed value is a typed config
#                      failure, not a silent default).
#
# NEIGHBOUR_EXPANSION_RADIUS  ADR-0049's retrieved-verse neighbourhood window:
#                      how many ordinals on each side of a verse already in
#                      context join the context (non-negative integer; `0`
#                      disables the expansion and a NEGATIVE value is a typed
#                      config failure when the chat wiring builds — the process
#                      boots, every `/v1/chat` request answers 503 — not a
#                      disable; absent = the domain default of 1; malformed =
#                      typed config failure).
#
# NEIGHBOUR_EXPANSION_CAP  How many chunks that neighbourhood expansion may add
#                      to one query (non-negative integer; `0` disables it and a
#                      NEGATIVE value is a typed config failure when the chat
#                      wiring builds — the process boots, every `/v1/chat`
#                      request answers 503 — not a disable; absent = the domain
#                      default of 12; malformed = typed config failure). Both
#                      knobs are what keep the widening bounded — uncapped, a
#                      radius of one adds a measured p50 of 46 chunks to a
#                      Quran-bearing query. They are independent budgets: a
#                      surah-naming Quran question can add SCOPE_EXPANSION_CAP
#                      plus NEIGHBOUR_EXPANSION_CAP chunks over the fused hits
#                      (24 at the defaults), which is the combined ceiling SPECS
#                      §5 prices.
#
# LABEL_LOOKUP_CAP     ADR-0058's citation-label lookup budget: the most chunks a
#                      question's own citation labels (a hadith collection + its
#                      number, an ayah's surah + ayah) may add over the fused hits
#                      (non-negative integer; `0` disables the lookup; absent = the
#                      domain default of 8; malformed = typed config failure). It is
#                      a third independent budget, so a query naming both a surah
#                      and a hadith can add up to all three caps.
#
# KAJIANQ_WEB_ROOT     where the disk ASSETS handle finds the shipped web
#                      build. The unit's WorkingDirectory is /srv/kajianq/api,
#                      so the default ("./apps/web/dist") would resolve to a
#                      path that does not exist on the deployed tree and every
#                      SPA route would 503 while /v1/health stays green — this
#                      line is load-bearing, not cosmetic. deploy.sh ships the
#                      web build to <KAJIANQ_DEPLOY_ROOT>/web, where that tree
#                      comes from the deploying machine's deploy.env
#                      (/srv/kajianq on this box), and this key must name that
#                      tree's web/ directory.

DATABASE_URL=postgres://kajianq:CHANGE_ME@127.0.0.1:5432/kajianq
APP_ENV=staging
ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://chat.example.org
SENTRY_DSN=
GEMINI_PAID_API_KEY=CHANGE_ME
GEMINI_API_KEY=CHANGE_ME
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=CHANGE_ME
DASHSCOPE_API_KEY=CHANGE_ME
OLLAMA_API_KEY=CHANGE_ME
JEV_API_KEY=CHANGE_ME
PROVIDER_PROFILE=default
SCOPE_EXPANSION_CAP=12
NEIGHBOUR_EXPANSION_RADIUS=1
NEIGHBOUR_EXPANSION_CAP=12
LABEL_LOOKUP_CAP=8
KAJIANQ_WEB_ROOT=/srv/kajianq/web